+# CVE-2026-78408 — False Positive Assessment for Debian Bookworm (util-linux)
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2026-78408 does not affect the util-linux package shipped in Debian Bookworm.**
+The bug is an `nsenter --join-cgroup` file-descriptor leak (`cgroup_procs_fd`
+left open across `setns` / `setuid` / `execve`). `--join-cgroup` was introduced in
+util-linux **v2.40**. Debian Bookworm ships **2.38.1**. There is nothing to patch.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+> nsenter `--join-cgroup` opens a file descriptor to `cgroup.procs` and can leave
+> that descriptor open across namespace and credential changes, leaking a
+> privileged cgroup control FD into the executed program.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2026-78408
+- **Advisory:** [GHSA-55fx-f4gg-cfhj](https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-55fx-f4gg-cfhj)
+- **Affected upstream:** util-linux **v2.40 through v2.42.2**
+- **Upstream fix commits:**
+  - `afe067c979b9ba2cbe856f7c6411210120ea62aa` (close the FD)
+  - `003c622428f09fc6544ed06b533d278dc14f88e0` (O_CLOEXEC)
+  - `485dbb67f1b6bb18e08b1b77f4aa2373ff3a705b` / `43ec8a89f6c99130727084b3496a2ffd2b4200f0` (v2.41)
+- **Debian security tracker:** https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78408
+
+---
+
+## Affected Package in Debian Bookworm
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Package | util-linux |
+| Bookworm version | `2.38.1-5+deb12u3` |
+| Upstream base | util-linux v2.38.1 |
+| Debian tracker status | Still listed as vulnerable (version-range, not yet `<not-affected>`) |
+
+---
+
+## Root Cause of the CVE
+
+`nsenter --join-cgroup` (added in v2.40, commit `b40650b`) opens `cgroup_procs_fd`
+and does not reliably close it / set `O_CLOEXEC` before dropping privileges and
+executing the target. The FD leak is the CVE.
+
+---
+
+## Why v2.38.1 (Debian Bookworm) Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. `--join-cgroup` does not exist in v2.38
+
+Red Hat documents that earlier releases, including util-linux 2.38, are not
+affected because the option was introduced in v2.40.
+
+### 2. Direct code verification
+
+```
+$ grep -n 'join-cgroup\|cgroup_procs_fd' sys-utils/nsenter.c
+(no output)
+```
+
+Bookworm `nsenter.c` has no `cgroup_procs_fd` and no `--join-cgroup` option.
+Debian's patch set does not add it.
+
+---
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Date | Event |
+|---|---|
+| 2022-08-04 | util-linux v2.38.1 released (Bookworm base) |
+| 2024 | v2.40 introduces `--join-cgroup` |
+| 2026 | CVE-2026-78408 assigned; FD close / O_CLOEXEC fixes landed |
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-78408 is a false positive for Debian Bookworm util-linux 2.38.1-5+deb12u3.**
+
+Scanners that match the Debian tracker version range will still flag it. Suppress
+the finding; no code patch is required.
+
+---
+
+## References
+
+- Upstream close-FD fix: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/afe067c979b9ba2cbe856f7c6411210120ea62aa
+- O_CLOEXEC: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/003c622428f09fc6544ed06b533d278dc14f88e0
+- GitHub advisory: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-55fx-f4gg-cfhj
+- Debian security tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78408
+- Debian Bookworm package: https://packages.debian.org/bookworm/util-linux
