+# CVE-2026-78409 — False Positive Assessment for Debian Bookworm (util-linux)
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2026-78409 does not affect the util-linux package shipped in Debian Bookworm.**
+The assigned bug is an `open_tree()` symlink escape on the Linux >= 6.15
+detached-tree fast path for `X-mount.subdir`. That path was introduced in
+util-linux **v2.42**. Debian Bookworm ships **2.38.1** with an older bind/pathname
+`X-mount.subdir` implementation and **no `open_tree()`**. There is nothing to patch.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+> libmount `X-mount.subdir` on the detached-tree (`open_tree`) path can follow
+> symlinks and escape the intended subdirectory, mounting a location the caller
+> did not specify.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2026-78409
+- **Advisory:** [GHSA-8f2p-47x3-43mv](https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-8f2p-47x3-43mv)
+- **Affected upstream:** util-linux **v2.42** detached-tree `X-mount.subdir` path
+  (introduced by `ae19f7546ccb`)
+- **Upstream fix commit:** `ed072cf2297b68f86af8e08209907f605dd42e5d`
+- **Debian security tracker:** https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78409
+
+---
+
+## Affected Package in Debian Bookworm
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Package | util-linux |
+| Bookworm version | `2.38.1-5+deb12u3` |
+| Upstream base | util-linux v2.38.1 |
+| Debian tracker status | Still listed as vulnerable (version-range, not yet `<not-affected>`) |
+
+---
+
+## Root Cause of the CVE
+
+On Linux >= 6.15, libmount can attach a detached mount tree via `open_tree()`.
+The v2.42 `X-mount.subdir` implementation resolved the subdirectory with
+`open_tree(api->fd_tree, subdir)` without `AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW`, allowing a
+symlink to escape the intended tree.
+
+---
+
+## Why v2.38.1 (Debian Bookworm) Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. The vulnerable code path was introduced in v2.42
+
+Bookworm 2.38.1 predates that implementation by several upstream major versions.
+
+### 2. Direct code verification
+
+```
+$ grep -n 'open_tree' libmount/src/*.c
+(no output)
+
+$ grep -n 'X-mount.subdir' libmount/src/context.c
+(older bind/pathname helper — not the detached open_tree path)
+```
+
+There is no `hook_mount.c` detached-subdir `open_tree()` call to backport into.
+
+### 3. Debian's patch set does not introduce the vulnerability
+
+`2.38.1-5+deb12u3` does not add the v2.42 detached-tree subdir path.
+
+---
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Date | Event |
+|---|---|
+| 2022-08-04 | util-linux v2.38.1 released (Bookworm base) |
+| 2025-04-15 | `ae19f7546ccb` introduces detached-tree X-mount.subdir (v2.42) |
+| 2026 | CVE-2026-78409 assigned; fix in ed072cf2 |
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-78409 is a false positive for Debian Bookworm util-linux 2.38.1-5+deb12u3.**
+
+The assigned `open_tree()` escape does not exist in 2.38.1. Scanners that follow
+the Debian tracker version range will still flag it. Suppress the finding; no
+code patch is required.
+
+---
+
+## References
+
